# The mirror stages every text file with LF endings (applyReplacements normalizes
# to LF before scrubbing). Without this, Git's autocrlf on a Windows checkout
# rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, so the next scheduled sync sees all ~64
# files as modified and commits line-ending-only churn every night.
#
# Normalize in the repo, and check out LF so the working tree matches what the
# mirror produces. That makes an unchanged sync a genuine no-op.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
